				},
				"description": "To authenticate with the DUKE.ai Backend, you must have a SDK client_id to begin with.\n\nGiven that you have a SDK client_id and your corresponding api_key, pass those in to the x-www-form-urlencoded body, along with the email address of the carrier that this is for: {{cust_id}}.\n\nThe email address of the carrier does not have to be an existing DUKE user, we take care of that part for you. This is how loads are compartmentalized in the DUKE.ai database to keep customer load data from intermingling.\n\nWhat is returned will be a set of AWS keys. The key pertinent to sending other requests for handling load data is the \"idToken\". If you understand Cognito, then you can use the \"access_token\" and \"refresh_token\" to refresh your token which expires after 30 minutes of inactivity. Otherwise, you can send the same request again to get a new \"idToken\"."
			},
